WEBVTT

00:16:29.196 --> 00:16:31.556
where you're going to be
confronted with this?

00:16:31.596 --> 00:16:34.436
L: Yeah, and I think
that happens all the time.

00:16:34.476 --> 00:16:36.916
Like, you know, I have an idea.

00:16:37.276 --> 00:16:38.756
Oh, but someone starts talking,

00:16:38.756 --> 00:16:41.956
and then like, you just sort of
fade back into the background,

00:16:41.996 --> 00:16:44.756
and that’s something
I want to counteract more often.

00:16:44.756 --> 00:16:48.156
Because, more often than not,

00:16:48.196 --> 00:16:49.996
you know that idea is a contribution,

00:16:50.036 --> 00:16:51.716
and why am I hesitating so much?

00:16:51.756 --> 00:16:53.036
DHP: Yeah.

00:16:53.036 --> 00:16:54.196
So you have a lesson.

00:16:54.236 --> 00:16:55.836
The lesson is, speak up.

00:16:55.876 --> 00:16:57.716
So why don't you --

00:16:57.756 --> 00:17:02.956
So how about the next meeting you're in,